{
  "name": "FFT Spectrogram (6 band)",
  "notes": "Port of `fft`. The animation maps every LED to a log-spaced FFT bin and colours it by that bin's level; this is the same thing at six bins instead of 512, because `SpectrumSignal` gives N outputs from one modulator slot and is on no list in `SignalNodes`, so no document can build one (LIFE-675). Six bands is what six of sixteen slots buys.\n\nColour by LEVEL is `paletteSpan` 0: the index collapses, `t = paletteOffset`, and one row per band paints its whole segment a single colour off the black-green-yellow-red ramp. That is the animation's palette exactly, and it is why this is the one port with no hue knob -- rotating the hue of a meter whose colours MEAN something is not a control anybody wants.\n\n`brightness` is `G.opacity`, the global stage. Six layers would otherwise need six rows for one knob, and the animation's brightness really is a property of the whole picture rather than of any band.\n\nBand edges are the animation's own: log-spaced from bin 2 to bin 486, which is its `minFreqBin` and `numBins * 0.95`.\n\n`log_scale` does not port. It is a toggle that rewrites each bin as dB before the gain stage, and a toggle is a structural choice no knob reaches; `audio_band` has no dB mode. `sensitivity` is capped too -- the animation declares 0.1-100 and the node stops at 30.",
